# ============================================================
#  Calendar: the academy year's fixed beats.
#  Most are `trigger: auto` — forced into the month's deck
#  whenever their `when` is true (and `repeat` allows).
#  Month 1 Harvestmoon ... 12 Starfall. 11–12 are summer recess.
# ============================================================

@event intro_arrival
title: The Sky-Barge
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
art: tower
tags: story
scene: A wooden barge with patched sails drifting between clouds toward seven impossibly tall towers above a mirror-still lake.
text: The barge drops through the clouds and there it is: Lumenhold, seven towers stitched together with bridges of light. A first-year beside you is quietly being sick over the side. A prefect with a ledger counts heads and frowns at yours.
> ok: Step onto the landing
  say: Your boots touch stone that hums faintly underfoot. Four years. Forty-eight moons.

@event choose_origin
title: Who Were You Before?
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
type: menu
art: mirror
tags: story
scene: A tall enchanted mirror in the entrance hall, showing a different version of the viewer in each pane.
text: The Sorting Mirror in the entrance hall does not sort you into anything. It simply asks, in a voice like cold water, who you were before you came here. It waits.
> noble: A younger child of minor nobility
  hint: Charm and a known name. 60 crowns from home now, and an allowance each later term, with strings attached.
  gain origin_noble
  say: The mirror shows you a crest you have tried to outgrow. It approves, faintly.
> scholar: A provincial scholarship student
  hint: Lore above all. 30 crowns now, and a stipend each later term while your grades hold.
  gain origin_scholar
  say: The mirror shows you a candle burning very late in a very small room.
> hedge: Raised by a marsh hedge-witch
  hint: Alchemy, some Arcana, good spirits. 15 crowns, and no money from home: you'll need a job.
  gain origin_hedge
  say: The mirror smells, briefly, of wet moss and woodsmoke. You feel at home.
> street: Raised on the streets of Port Calder
  hint: Guile and grit. 8 crowns, and no one to send more: you'll need a job.
  gain origin_street
  say: The mirror shows a pickpocket's quick hands. You check your pockets out of habit.
> merchant: The heir to a trading company
  hint: The biggest purse and a nose for bargains: 120 crowns now, and more from the company when trade is good.
  gain origin_merchant
  say: The mirror shows ledgers, ships and your mother's disappointed face. Still: gold.

@event sorting_mirror
title: The Sorting Mirror
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
art: mirror
tags: story
scene: A tall enchanted mirror in the entrance hall, showing a different version of the viewer in each pane.
text: The Sorting Mirror in the entrance hall does not sort you into anything. It simply asks, in a voice like cold water, who you were before you came here. You tell it.
> ok: Look into the mirror
  say: {has(origin_noble): The mirror shows you a crest you have tried to outgrow. It approves, faintly.|{has(origin_scholar): The mirror shows you a candle burning very late in a very small room.|{has(origin_hedge): The mirror smells, briefly, of wet moss and woodsmoke. You feel at home.|{has(origin_street): The mirror shows a pickpocket's quick hands. You check your pockets out of habit.|The mirror shows ledgers, ships and your mother's disappointed face. Still: gold.}}}}

@event wrapup_begins
title: The Last Weeks
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: wrapup and month == 11
priority: 70
art: tower
tags: story
scene: An emptying castle in late summer light, trunks stacked in a corridor, a notice pinned to the great hall door.
text: A notice on the great hall door: classes are over, duties are done, and final-years may stay on until graduation, board on the house. The castle is yours for one last summer.
> ok: Make the most of it
  mood +small
  say: You walk the long way to breakfast, past every door you ever got lost behind.

@event choose_elective
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 1 or month == 6"); replaced by enrolment (offers: courses, pick: 2)
title: Choosing an Elective
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 5
priority: 45
type: menu
art: scroll
tags: study class retired
scene: A long noticeboard covered in fluttering enchanted parchment, each sheet trying to shoulder the others aside.
text: The registrar's noticeboard flaps with sign-up sheets for this term's electives. Core lectures are compulsory; your elective is yours to choose. The sheets jostle for your attention.
> pyro: Pyromancy
  hint: +Arcana each month, small burns. Taught by Professor Thorne.
  gain class_pyromancy
> tide: Tidecalling
  hint: +Arcana, +Vigor, lakeside calm.
  gain class_tidecalling
> illusion: Illusion & Glamour
  hint: +Guile, +Charm.
  gain class_illusion
> alchemy: Practical Alchemy
  hint: +Alchemy.
  gain class_alchemy
> divination: Divination
  hint: +Lore, occasional gloomy omens.
  gain class_divination
> artifice: Artifice
  hint: +Alchemy, +Lore.
  gain class_artifice
> beast: Beastcraft
  hint: +Vigor, +Mood. Smells of hay.
  gain class_beastcraft
> astro: Astromancy
  hint: +Lore, late nights.
  gain class_astromancy
> healing: Healing Arts
  hint: +Alchemy, +Lore, a little health.
  gain class_healing
> umbral: Umbral Theory (restricted)
  hint: Requires Lore 20 or second year. +Arcana, dark moods.
  when: lore >= 20 or year >= 2
  locked: Needs Lore 20, or your second year.
  gain class_umbral
  flag took_umbral

@event club_fair
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 2"); replaced by club_fair_v3 (offers: clubs)
title: The Club Fair
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 12
priority: 40
type: menu
art: group
tags: social club retired
scene: The great courtyard filled with banners and stalls: a duelist juggling sparks, a choir floating a foot off the ground, a girl handing out newspapers that shout headlines.
text: The courtyard is a riot of banners. Every club wants you, or at least your membership fee. A broom whizzes overhead trailing a SKYRACE TRYOUTS banner; somewhere a choir is harmonising with a cat.
> duel: Dueling Circle
  hint: +Vigor +Arcana, bruises. Home of the Spring Tournament.
  gain club_dueling
  meet lyra
> choir: Choir of the Spheres
  hint: +Charm, +Mood.
  gain club_choir
> sky: Skyrace Squad
  hint: +Vigor, crowd glory, crashes.
  gain club_skyrace
> ledger: The Lumen Ledger
  hint: +Guile +Charm. Nessa Quill's student paper.
  gain club_ledger
  meet nessa
> garden: Verdant Circle
  hint: +Alchemy +Mood. Greenhouses and gossip.
  gain club_garden
  meet tobias
> stars: Stargazers
  hint: +Lore +Mood.
  gain club_stargazers
> none: Keep your evenings free
  hint: No club (leaves your current club, if any).
  lose club_dueling
  lose club_choir
  lose club_skyrace
  lose club_ledger
  lose club_garden
  lose club_stargazers
  mood +tiny

@event job_board
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 3 or month == 9"); replaced by job_board_visit (the Job Board place)
title: The Job Board
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 5
priority: 35
type: menu
art: coin
tags: job money retired
scene: A cork board outside the bursar's office, papered with notices; one is on fire, one is wriggling.
text: Rent is ten crowns a month and your purse is a fragile thing. The board outside the bursar's office offers honest work, and some that is merely work.
> library: Library Assistant — 10 gold/month
  hint: +Lore, a little dull.
  gain job_library
> tavern: The Gilded Newt — 16 gold/month
  hint: +Charm, tiring evenings in the village.
  gain job_tavern
> apothecary: Apothecary Clerk — 12 gold/month
  hint: Requires Alchemy 12. +Alchemy.
  when: alchemy >= 12
  locked: Needs Alchemy 12.
  gain job_apothecary
> stables: Familiar Stables — 11 gold/month
  hint: +Vigor. Things bite.
  gain job_stables
> tutor: First-Year Tutor — 12 gold/month
  hint: Requires Lore 18. +Standing.
  when: lore >= 18
  locked: Needs Lore 18.
  gain job_tutor
> courier: Broom Courier — 18 gold/month
  hint: Requires Vigor 14. Dangerous.
  when: vigor >= 14
  locked: Needs Vigor 14.
  gain job_courier
> none: No job (quit any current one)
  lose job_library
  lose job_tavern
  lose job_apothecary
  lose job_stables
  lose job_tutor
  lose job_courier

@event lantern_night
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 2"); replaced by lantern_night_v3 (a festival at the lakeshore)
title: Lantern Night
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 12
art: lantern
tags: festival social retired
scene: Hundreds of paper lanterns rising off the lake at dusk, each with a wish written on it in glowing ink.
text: On Lantern Night every student writes a wish on a paper lantern and lets it go over the lake. Rumour says the lanterns that sink were wishes the lake wanted for itself.
> left: Wish for something selfish
  chance even:
    gold +large
    say: Your lantern rises high. The next morning you find coins in your shoe. The lake is generous, and a little creepy.
  else:
    mood -small
    say: Your lantern sinks with a hiss. Something under the water now knows what you want.
    flag lake_knows
    alignment -small
> right: Wish for someone else
  alignment +tiny
  mood +medium
  renown +small
  say: Your lantern rises and catches the wind. Across the shore, someone you have never met laughs out loud for no reason.

@event kael_arrives
title: The Boy From the North
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: auto
when: turn == 3
priority: 30
actor: kael
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A pale young man in a fur-lined coat standing at the door of the dining hall, frost spreading from his boots across the floor.
text: Mid-term, the dining hall doors open and frost crawls across the floor. A boy in a fur coat walks in, takes the empty seat beside you, and says nothing at all. The headmistress introduces him as Kael Dumont, a transfer. She does not say from where.
> left: Leave him be
  meet kael
  rel kael +tiny
  say: You eat in silence. When you leave, your cup of tea has frozen solid.
> right: Offer him the bread
  meet kael
  rel kael +medium
  say: He looks at the bread as if no one has offered him anything in a long time. "...Thank you." His voice sounds like wind over snow.
  flag kael_kindness

@event winter_trials
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 4"); replaced by term-end exams (engine, design §7.3)
title: The Winter Trials
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 12
priority: 40
art: hourglass
tags: study exam retired
scene: A vast examination hall where floating quills hover over a hundred desks and the windows are thick with frost.
text: The Winter Trials. A hundred desks, a hundred floating quills, one very old proctor who may be asleep. The first question asks you to explain the Third Law of Correspondence. The second asks you to demonstrate it.
> left: Lean on theory
  challenge research journeyman:
    win:
      study +large
      mood +small
      say: Your answer is so thorough the quill gets a cramp. Top marks.
    lose:
      study -large
      mood -small
      say: You write three pages and realise halfway that you have been answering a different question.
> right: Lean on practice
  challenge spell journeyman:
    win:
      study +large
      renown +small
      say: Your demonstration is clean and bright. The proctor wakes up and applauds.
    lose:
      study -large
      health -small
      say: The demonstration backfires. Politely, but with smoke.

@event midwinter_ball
slot: evening
title: The Midwinter Ball
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: month == 4
repeat: 12
priority: 40
type: menu
art: music
tags: festival romance social
scene: The great hall transformed: an ice-crystal chandelier, couples waltzing a foot above the floor, snow falling indoors without ever landing.
text: The great hall has been turned to ice and starlight for the Midwinter Ball. Couples float above the floor. Who will you go with? You can only ask someone you know well.
> lyra: Ask Lyra
  when: met(lyra) and rel(lyra) >= 9
  hint: {&She has had six invitations. She hasn't said yes to any.|She has had invitations again. She is pretending not to count them.}
  challenge appeal vs lyra.charm +1 if spark(lyra) >= 25:
    win:
      spark lyra +medium
      rel lyra +medium
      mood +medium
      queue ball_last_dance now with lyra
      say: {bond(lyra) == "partner": "Obviously," she says, before you finish asking. She leads, of course.|{flag(ball_lyra): "Again? Fine. You've improved." She dances like a duel, and this year you nearly keep up.|"Finally, someone who doesn't stammer." She dances like a duel — and wins.}}
      flag ball_lyra
    lose:
      rel lyra -small
      mood -small
      say: "I'm going alone. It's more efficient." You watch her dance alone all night, perfectly.
> tobias: Ask Tobias
  when: met(tobias) and rel(tobias) >= 9
  hint: {flag(ball_tobias): He has been practising with a broom again. The broom has improved.|He has been practising with a broom.}
  spark tobias +medium
  rel tobias +medium
  mood +medium
  queue ball_last_dance now with tobias
  say: {flag(ball_tobias): He only steps on your feet twice this year, and is so proud of it that he tells everyone. It's the best night of the term.|He steps on your feet nine times and apologises ten. It's the best night of the term.}
  flag ball_tobias
> seraphine: Ask Seraphine
  when: met(seraphine) and rel(seraphine) >= 9
  hint: She may already know you'll ask.
  spark seraphine +medium
  rel seraphine +medium
  mood +medium
  queue ball_last_dance now with seraphine
  say: {flag(ball_seraphine): "Same as last time," Seraphine says, "but you'll wear blue." You hadn't planned to. You do.|"I said yes three weeks ago," she says, "you just hadn't asked yet." She dances a beat ahead of the music.}
  flag ball_seraphine
> corvin: Ask Corvin
  when: met(corvin) and rel(corvin) >= 9
  hint: Odds he shows up: unclear.
  chance likely:
    spark corvin +medium
    mood +medium
    queue ball_last_dance now with corvin
    say: {flag(ball_corvin): He arrives on time, which alarms everyone, in a jacket he swears is borrowed. He is still the best dancer in the room.|He arrives late, in a stolen jacket, and is the best dancer in the room.}
    flag ball_corvin
  else:
    mood -medium
    say: {flag(ball_corvin_arrested): He never shows. A note arrives at midnight: "Not arrested this time. Worse. Explain later." He never does.|He never shows. A note arrives at midnight: "Got arrested. Long story. Save me a dance next year."}
    flag ball_corvin_arrested
> mir: Ask Mir
  when: met(mir) and rel(mir) >= 9
  hint: {flag(ball_mir): They promise the violin has been fixed.|They're bringing a self-playing violin.}
  spark mir +medium
  rel mir +small
  mood +medium
  say: {flag(ball_mir): The violin behaves all night. Mir is almost disappointed, until it plays the last waltz entirely on its own and bows.|Mir's violin plays itself, then plays the chandelier, then plays the windows. You are asked to leave early. Worth it.}
  flag ball_mir
> kael: Ask Kael
  when: met(kael) and rel(kael) >= 12
  hint: He doesn't seem to feel the cold.
  spark kael +medium
  rel kael +medium
  mood +medium
  queue ball_last_dance now with kael
  say: {flag(ball_kael): He takes your hand without asking this time, as if it were already decided. The frost-ferns on the glass grow into a whole winter garden.|He holds your hand like it is something fragile. Where your fingers touch, frost-ferns bloom on the glass.}
  flag ball_kael
> nessa: Ask Nessa
  when: met(nessa) and rel(nessa) >= 9
  hint: She'll be working. She's always working.
  spark nessa +medium
  rel nessa +medium
  renown +small
  queue ball_last_dance now with nessa
  say: {flag(ball_nessa): She leaves her notebook in her bag all night. "The column can make something up," she says. It does.|She takes notes between dances. "For the society column." Then she stops taking notes.}
  flag ball_nessa
> friends: Go with friends
  mood +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: {flag(ball_friends): You go as a pack again, and this year someone has taught everyone the same dance, badly. It is still perfect.|You go as a pack and dance badly together and it is perfect.}
  flag ball_friends
> skip: Stay in and study
  lore +small
  study +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: The music drifts up through the floor while you read. Somewhere, people are happy. You are productive.

@event spring_tournament
title: The Spring Tournament
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: auto
when: month == 8 and not member(duelling)
repeat: 12
priority: 40
art: duel
tags: festival rival
chain: tournament
scene: A ring of white stone on the lawn, crowds in the stands, two duelists bowing as their wands spark.
text: The Spring Tournament: dueling on the great lawn, the whole academy watching. Entry is open to anyone foolish enough.
> left: Watch from the stands
  mood +small
  say: You eat candied chestnuts and scream for strangers.
> right: Enter the tournament
  challenge combat journeyman+ drift mid:
    win:
      renown +medium
      say: First round: you win, barely, and {flag(tournament_champion): the crowd remembers your name from last year and chants it.|the crowd learns your name.}
      queue tournament_semifinal now
    lose:
      health -medium
      renown +tiny
      say: First round: you are knocked out of the ring before you've found your footing. The crowd has already turned to the next bout.

@event spring_tournament_circle
title: The Spring Tournament
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: auto
when: month == 8 and member(duelling)
repeat: 12
priority: 40
chain: tournament
art: duel
tags: rival
scene: The great lawn ringed with banners, a chalk duelling circle at its centre and the Duelling Circle's names on a board.
text: The Spring Tournament: duelling on the great lawn, the whole academy watching. The Duelling Circle's names went up on the board a week ago, yours among them. {rank(duelling) >= 3: You are the captain, and the Circle expects its captain to win something.|The captain wants results, and says so.}
> left: Fight to make a good showing
  challenge combat journeyman drift mid:
    win:
      renown +small
      perform duelling +small
      say: You win your first bout cleanly and lose the second honourably. {rank(duelling) >= 3: Your second-years cheer their captain louder than anyone in the stands.|The captain ticks your name, which from her is a medal.}
    lose:
      health -small
      say: You go out in the first round, on your feet at least. {rank(duelling) >= 3: Your second-years are kind about it, which is worse.|The captain says you fought like someone who expected to lose.}
> right: Go for the title
  challenge combat journeyman+ drift mid:
    win:
      renown +medium
      say: First round: you win, barely, and the crowd learns your name.
      queue tournament_semifinal now
    lose:
      health -medium
      renown +tiny
      perform duelling -tiny
      say: First round: you are knocked out of the ring before you've found your footing, and the Circle's bench goes very quiet.

@event tournament_semifinal
title: Semifinal
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: queued
art: duel
tags: rival
chain: tournament
scene: The same ring at sunset, scorch marks on the stone. Your opponent is grinning.
text: The semifinal. Your opponent is a fourth-year who has never lost. The crowd is louder now; you can hear your own name in it.
> left: Fight clean
  challenge combat expert- drift mid:
    win:
      renown +medium
      say: You trade spells like questions and answers — and get the last word.
      queue tournament_final now
    lose:
      health -medium
      renown +small
      say: A good fight. Not good enough. The crowd applauds you off the lawn.
> right: Fight dirty
  alignment -small
  challenge deceive adept drift mid:
    win:
      renown +small
      say: A feint, a trip, a jinx to the shoelaces. Legal. Mostly.{met(bram):  On the prefects' bench Bram watches the whole thing with his jaw set, and doesn't clap.|}
      queue tournament_final now
      if met(bram):
        rel bram -small
    lose:
      renown -small
      say: The referee sees the trick. Disqualified, and booed.

@event tournament_final
title: The Final
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: queued
art: trophy
tags: rival festival
chain: tournament
scene: The dueling ring under floating lanterns, a silver cup on a plinth, and across from you, a familiar face.
text: The final. Across the ring stands {lyra}, wand raised, eyes blazing. "I was hoping it would be you," she says, and she is not being friendly.
> left: Give everything you have
  meet lyra
  challenge combat vs lyra.arcana +3:
    win:
      renown +huge
      mood +large
      flag tournament_champion
      gain famous
      rel lyra -medium
      if bond(lyra) == "none":
        bond lyra rival
      say: Your final spell lands like a bell. Silence — then the lawn erupts. Lyra stares at you as if seeing you for the first time, then walks off the lawn without shaking your hand.
    lose:
      renown +medium
      rel lyra +small
      say: She wins, but only just. Afterwards, she offers her hand. "Next year," she says. It is a promise and a threat.
> right: Yield with a bow
  meet lyra
  rel lyra +large
  renown +small
  mood -tiny
  say: The crowd boos. Lyra does not cheer her victory. Later she finds you: "Why?" You don't have a good answer, and she seems to like that.

@event grand_exams
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 10"); replaced by term-end exams (engine, design §7.3)
title: Grand Examinations
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 12
priority: 40
art: scroll
tags: study exam retired
scene: A circular examination chamber with a domed ceiling of moving constellations; examiners in grey robes sit behind a long table.
text: Year-end examinations. Three days, five examiners and a practical in front of a panel that includes the headmistress. Your standing for the year rides on this.
> left: Prepare a dazzling practical
  challenge spell adept+:
    win:
      study +large
      renown +small
      say: You finish your practical and the examiners actually lean forward. Distinction.
    lose:
      study -huge
      mood -medium
      say: The practical sputters. An examiner writes something very short.
> right: Write a meticulous thesis
  challenge research adept+:
    win:
      study +large
      mood +small
      say: Your thesis is cited by one examiner in an argument with another. Distinction.
    lose:
      study -huge
      mood -medium
      say: Your thesis is described, aloud, as "ambitious". It is not a compliment.

@event summer_plans
# retired in phase 2b (was "month == 11"); replaced by break_plan
title: Summer Recess
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: false
repeat: 12
priority: 40
type: menu
art: sun
tags: home retired
scene: The academy gates thrown open to green hills; students with trunks waving from departing sky-barges.
text: The towers empty for the summer. Two months of freedom. How will you spend them?
> home: Go home
  hint: Rest and recover. No rent while away.
  gain summer_away
  health +large
  mood +large
  if has(origin_noble):
    say: Your family hosts three dinners in your honour and asks about your marriage prospects at all of them.
  elif has(origin_street):
    say: The old crowd in Port Calder treats you like a returning hero, and steals your trunk only once.
  else:
    say: Home is smaller than you remember, and warmer. Someone made your favourite pie.
> work: Take summer work in the village
  hint: About 50 gold over the summer. Tiring.
  gain summer_work
  vigor +small
  say: You haul crates, serve tables and polish brass until your hands know the shape of every coin.
> study: Stay and study in the empty library
  hint: +Lore, +Arcana, +Standing. Lonely.
  lore +medium
  arcana +medium
  study +small
  mood -small
  say: Just you, the books and the dust motes. You learn things the term never had time for.
> travel: Travel to the coast
  hint: Costs 40 gold. Great for mood.
  when: gold >= 40
  locked: Needs 40 crowns.
  gold -large
  gain summer_away
  mood +huge
  charm +small
  say: Salt air, shell markets, a sea serpent at sunset. You come back tanned and ten years younger.
> expedition: Join Old Maud's herb expedition
  hint: Requires knowing Maud. Adventure.
  when: met(maud)
  gain summer_away
  alchemy +medium
  vigor +small
  rel maud +large
  health +small
  say: Two months in the Whisperwood with Maud and her goat. You learn which mushrooms sing and which ones lie.

@event summer_letter
title: A Letter From Home
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: month == 12 and not has(summer_away) and not wrapup
repeat: 12
art: letter
tags: home
scene: A letter sealed with candle wax lying on a sunlit windowsill.
text: A letter arrives in the last month of summer, the handwriting so familiar it hurts. They want to know how you are doing. Really doing.
> left: Write back honestly
  mood +small
  if (turn > 4 and gpa < 2.0):
    mood -medium
    say: You tell them about your grades. Their reply is kind, which is worse.
  else:
    say: You write six pages. It feels like setting down a heavy bag.
> right: Write back that everything is perfect
  mood -tiny
  guile +tiny
  alignment -tiny
  chance even:
    gold +medium
    say: Proud of you, they write, and enclose a little money{has(origin_noble) or has(origin_merchant): , as if a purse were the right answer to a letter.|  you suspect they couldn't spare.}
  else:
    say: They reply with exclamation marks. The lie sits in your stomach all week.

@event starfall
slot: night
title: Starfall
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: month == 12 and year < 4 and not off_campus
repeat: 12
priority: 30
type: menu
art: star
tags: festival
scene: Students lying on the observatory roof under a sky streaked with falling stars.
text: {year == 1: The last night of the academic year. Everyone climbs onto the observatory roof, and the rest spill out onto the lawns with blankets, to watch the stars fall. They say if you catch one in a jar, you get a year of luck.|Starfall again. The observatory roof, the lawns full of blankets, the whole academy lying on its back.} {starfall_jar >= 1: Your jar is ready, cork in hand.|} {~The first star falls before anyone is ready.|Somebody has brought a lute, unwisely.|The lake is full of reflected stars.}
> left: Lie back and just watch
  mood +medium
  health +small
  starfall_jar = 0
  say: You count forty falling stars and then stop counting. It's enough.
> right: Try to catch a star
  hint: Nobody has caught one in years. A good jar from the observatory improves the odds.
  if starfall_jar >= 1:
    challenge feat apprentice unlikely luck:
      win:
        renown +small
        mood +small
        gain inspired
        queue starfall_caught
        say: It lands in your jar with a hiss and glows for weeks. Students come to see it.
      lose:
        health -small
        say: You lunge, miss, and nearly roll off the roof. A prefect catches you by the collar.
  else:
    challenge feat apprentice slim luck:
      win:
        renown +small
        mood +small
        gain inspired
        queue starfall_caught
        say: It lands in your jar with a hiss and glows for weeks. Students come to see it.
      lose:
        health -small
        say: You lunge, miss, and nearly roll off the roof. A prefect catches you by the collar.
  starfall_jar = 0
> together: Find your sweetheart on the lawn
  when: bonds_around(partner) > 0
  starfall_jar = 0
  queue starfall_together now
  say: You leave the roof and go looking. You know exactly where to look.
> wish: Make the Starfall wish
  starfall_jar = 0
  queue starfall_wish now
  say: You climb to the very top of the roof, where the old custom says the wishes go.

@event year_two
title: Second Year
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: turn == 13
priority: 55
art: tower
tags: story
scene: The seven towers in autumn colours, the first-year barge arriving below, tiny and nervous.
text: The barge brings new first-years, and you watch them gawp at the towers. Was that really you a year ago? You know which staircases move now, and which professors you can charm. Second-years, a prefect announces, may apply for summer research posts in Stormbloom.{chosen(break_plan, home):  Your trunk still smells of home, and there's a cake in it you were told to share.|}
> ok: Begin the second year
  mood +small
  renown +small
  say: You unpack faster than last year, and in the right order. Someone in your year already has a list of the research posts, and the castle's midnight doors, side by side.

@event term_begins
title: The Spring Term
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: term and month == 7
repeat: 4
priority: 85
art: tower
tags: story
scene: The castle steps after the winter break, trunks stacked by the doors and the first lamps lit in the towers.
text: {chosen(break_plan, home): You come back from home with a tin of something your family insists you'll need, and the castle feels enormous after a winter of small rooms.|{chosen(break_plan, work): Your holiday wages are in your purse and your feet still ache from earning them. The castle fills up around you, trunk by trunk.|After a winter of empty corridors, the castle fills up around you again, and the noise of it is almost too much.}} The spring term begins, and the registrar's hall is already queueing.
> left: Get a head start on the reading
  lore +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You find a window seat in the library before the term has properly started. By the time the others arrive, you have a list of questions and a crick in your neck.
> right: Catch up with everyone first
  mood +small
  gold -tiny
  say: You spend the first evening in the common room, then at the Newt, hearing everyone's winter. The reading can wait a day. It waits three.

@event year_three
title: Third Year
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: turn == 25
priority: 55
art: crown
tags: story
scene: The headmistress addressing a hall of third-years, every candle in the room leaning toward her.
text: "Third years," the headmistress says, "you are past the middle of your time here. Next year will ask a great deal of you; spend this one finding out what you want from it." She looks, for a moment, directly at you.{chosen(break_plan, home):  You came straight from home, and the summer's quiet is still on you.|}
> ok: Begin the third year
  mood +tiny
  study +tiny
  say: You know the castle well enough now to get lost in it on purpose. This is the last year for a summer research post, and the holiday notices by the gates pay better every year.

# Marrow asks again (feedback 2026-10-20): the answer you gave her at the Welcome (intro_what_is_just), read back on the eve
# of graduation, and whether the four years kept to it, by where your alignment ended up: mercy is Lumen, fairness the
# middle, keeping your own safe Hollow. It changes nothing; it only remembers.
@event isolde_asks_again
slot: evening
title: Ask Me Again
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns and (flag(just_mercy) or flag(just_fair) or flag(just_strong))
priority: 65
art: scales
tags: story
scene: A grey-haired headmistress in an evening cloister holding a small worn notebook open, a final-year in graduation robes beside her.
text: Headmistress Marrow finds you in the cloister, the same small notebook under her arm, four years more worn. "I asked you what was just," she says, and reads it back: {flag(just_mercy): "Mercy."|{flag(just_fair): "Fairness."|"Keeping your own safe."}} She looks at you over the page. {(flag(just_mercy) and alignment >= 20) or (flag(just_fair) and alignment > -20 and alignment < 20) or (flag(just_strong) and alignment <= -20): "You kept to it. I watched."|"You changed your answer without telling me. Most people do."} "Well? I'm asking again."
> left: Give the same answer
  say: {(flag(just_mercy) and alignment >= 20) or (flag(just_fair) and alignment > -20 and alignment < 20) or (flag(just_strong) and alignment <= -20): You say it again, and this time you know what it cost. She writes it under the first, in the same hand. "Good," she says. "Some answers are worth giving twice."|You say it again, though you both know the four years said something else. She writes it down anyway. "Then go and live up to it," she says. "You've time. Not much, but some."}
> right: Give a new answer
  say: You tell her what four years taught you instead. She listens to all of it, writes it under the first, and closes the notebook on both. "That," she says, "is what I hoped the castle would do to you."

@event graduation_eve
slot: night
title: The Eve of Graduation
class: story
tone: light
trigger: auto
when: turn == max_turns
priority: 60
art: crown
tags: story
scene: Graduation robes laid out on a dormitory bed, a single candle burning, the towers lit gold outside the window.
text: Tomorrow you graduate. Your robes are laid out on the bed, slightly too long. Outside, the towers are lit gold. Four years have gone like a single held breath.
> left: Spend the night with friends
  mood +medium
  say: {bonds(friend) + bonds(close) + bonds(partner) > 0: Laughter until dawn. Promises to write. Some of them, you'll keep.|You knock on a few doors. Nobody who answers is a close friend, not yet, but they pour you a cup and keep you up laughing till dawn. You trade addresses anyway.}
> right: Walk the halls alone one last time
  lore +small
  mood +small
  say: Every corridor holds a memory. At the end of the last one, the castle sighs, as if saying goodbye.
